  "historical_output_text": " The post will not contain specific brand mentions.\n\nIn today like all the ones, my usual morning began in a small, bustling kitchen, with a pot brewing steadily and an array spread open on what was, on a better-fitted night, my coffee tabletop: stacks for each of breakfast and the daily newspapers to read. It dawn-ed when an unexpected visitor to that stack made my fingers tingly.\n\nI found the old notebook tucked under the last newspaper, hidden under the stack's bottommost pages like the shy child of an overeagar crowd, its spine barely visible from my initial glimpse of papers only, as it always was. It's an antique relic in the age I keep, the type my parents would likely recognize but my grandparents may have held, the leather binding cracked like the edges of my patience in these days. Each page held the scri",
